{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["The procurement and receiving demo uses mock source data through a documented adapter; a live connector awaits identification of the source system and interface (ASM-1, ASM-23).","Repeated source imports are matched by source identifiers, and PO lines and lots can split across lots and pens with allocated animal quantities retained (ASM-2, ASM-24, ASM-25).","Forecasts use configurable yard target-weight and expected-gain defaults with optional lot overrides (ASM-3).","Configured wastage applies to estimates and projections; actual known wastage is a separate movement, while actual stock consumption is based on delivered quantity (ASM-4, ASM-28, ASM-34).","Ration optimization compares candidate mixes against user-selected nutritional requirements, displays the lowest-cost qualifying mix, and saves only when the user chooses (ASM-5, ASM-29).","A saved plan remains unchanged and is flagged for review after relevant inputs change; an authorized user confirms or regenerates it (ASM-7, ASM-30).","When stock is insufficient, the feeding save is refused and the web app presents the returned error (ASM-9, ASM-31).","Feed calculations use as-fed quantities; feed totals are converted to pounds for feed-to-gain metrics and dry matter is used for nutrition calculations (ASM-20, ASM-34).","A projected ship date uses the current date plus remaining target weight divided by positive ADG and is unavailable without positive ADG (ASM-13, ASM-33).","Date-range report metrics use feeding and weight records in the selected range; sex is retained when supplied and its filter is unavailable for records without sex data (ASM-21, ASM-35).","Dashboard lot rankings use a user-selected measure; dashboards remain summary-only and lot/report screens provide detail (ASM-22, ASM-36).","Predictive suggestions are explainable rule-based recommendations and do not change saved plans unless a user chooses an action (ASM-18, ASM-19).","Sample records remain distinguishable from operational records, duplicate loading is prevented, and reset or replacement requires confirmation (ASM-15, ASM-37).","Yard summary ADG and cost of gain aggregate from total gain and total feed cost across included lots (ASM-38).","Access-aware screen actions and displayed values follow permissions returned for the signed-in user; the request's role descriptions do not define additional role names or permissions beyond the answers (Q-1 through Q-8, ASM-6, ASM-8, ASM-11, ASM-12, ASM-14, ASM-16)."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths of 360 px, 768 px, and 1280 px, 100% of pages render without horizontal overflow; interactive controls at 360 px width have a minimum 44-by-44 CSS-pixel target.","text":"Every page shall render responsively at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."}],"outOfScope":["I-1 live procurement-system connector is deferred; the demo uses a documented mock-data import adapter (ASM-1, ASM-23)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed and the authentication service returns a valid user and permissions for submitted credentials","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the operational landing page and navigation actions allowed by the returned permissions","when":"The user submits the email and password"},{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed and the authentication service refuses the submitted credentials","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows an error message and remains on the sign-in page","when":"The user submits the email and password"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in and render navigation and actions from the signed-in user's returned permissions.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-9","Q-2"],"stability":0.86},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user with operational access opens the mock import screen and the adapter returns procurement and receiving records","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each returned record's vendor, source identifier, cost, head count, animal weight, breed, age, and source value","when":"The user starts an import"},{"given":"A user without operational access opens the import screen","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays imported records and does not show an import action","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"Where the mock import adapter is available, the feedlot web app shall let users with operational access import procurement and receiving records and view the returned vendor, source identifier, cost, head count, animal weight, breed, age, and source values.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-23","ASM-24","Q-3"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user with operational access views an imported PO line with a quantity that is allocated across two lots and those lots are allocated across pens","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen link with its allocated animal quantity","when":"The user saves the mappings and the service returns the mapped records"},{"given":"A user without operational access views the mapping screen","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays existing mappings and does not show mapping-change actions","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users with operational access map PO lines to one or more lots and lots to one or more pens with allocated animal quantities, and display the resulting PO-to-lot-to-pen traceability.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-2","ASM-25","Q-3"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has incoming animal data and the forecast service returns a target weight and market date","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned target-weight and market-date values with the lot's forecast basis","when":"A user opens the lot forecast"},{"given":"A user has manager permission and the forecast screen is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-4.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned forecast values for the updated assumptions","when":"The user changes a yard default or lot-specific override and saves it"},{"given":"A user does not have manager permission and the forecast screen is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-4.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays forecast values and does not show assumption-edit actions","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display market-date and target-weight forecasts based on incoming animal data and let authorized managers edit yard defaults and lot-specific forecast overrides.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-3","Q-4"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The inventory service returns feed items and their stock movements","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each item's name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, opening stock, received stock, consumed stock, and closing stock","when":"A user opens the inventory screen"},{"given":"A user has inventory permission and the inventory screen is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the values returned for the saved inventory record and stock movement","when":"The user records a receipt or adjustment, edits an item, or changes the wastage setting"},{"given":"A user lacks inventory permission and opens the inventory screen","id":"AC-REQ-5.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays inventory values and does not show inventory-maintenance actions","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display feed inventory items and stock movements and let authorized inventory users maintain items, record receipts or adjustments, and change the wastage setting.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-28","ASM-34","Q-5"],"stability":0.82},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The projection service returns estimates based on saved upcoming feed plans and the configured wastage ratio","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned projected consumption and closing inventory for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons","when":"A user selects each supported projection horizon"},{"given":"The inventory service returns a known actual-wastage movement and delivered-feed consumption","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows actual wastage as a separate movement from delivered-feed consumption","when":"A user opens the stock movement list"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display inventory projections for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons using the configured wastage ratio for estimates and projections while presenting known actual wastage as a separate stock movement.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-27","ASM-28"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has ration-management permission and the ration editor is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned ingredient mix, ration nutrition values, and cost per pound","when":"The user enters ingredients and their proportions and saves the ration"},{"given":"A user with ration-management permission has candidate mixes and user-selected nutrition requirements","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned lowest-cost candidate that meets the selected requirements and a separate action to save that candidate","when":"The user runs optimization"},{"given":"A user lacks ration-management permission and opens the ration screen","id":"AC-REQ-7.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays ration definitions and does not show create, revise, optimize, or approve actions","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users with ration-management permission create, revise, optimize, and approve ration definitions and display ingredient-mix nutrition and cost values.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-5","ASM-6","ASM-29","Q-6"],"stability":0.8},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has planning permission and the service returns a pen's animal count, bunk rate, and ration assignment","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned plan with date, pen, assigned lot or lots, animal count, ration, planned quantity, planned time, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and status","when":"The user generates a feed plan for a date"},{"given":"A saved plan's pen count, bunk rate, or ration assignment changes after plan generation","id":"AC-REQ-8.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the saved plan unchanged and displays a review flag with authorized confirm or regenerate actions","when":"The plan screen receives the changed inputs"},{"given":"An operator has execution-status permission for an assigned pen","id":"AC-REQ-8.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the status returned for that pen's plan","when":"The operator changes the plan status"},{"given":"A user lacks planning permission and opens the feed-plan screen","id":"AC-REQ-8.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays existing plans and does not show plan-generation or plan-adjustment actions","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let authorized planners generate or adjust dated pen-level feed plans from bunk rates, ration assignments, and animal counts, and let operators update execution status for their assigned pens.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-7","ASM-8","ASM-20","ASM-30","Q-7"],"stability":0.8},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user with operational feeding access opens a feeding activity form","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the saved activity with returned feed cost, energy value, inventory consumption, and lot-level cumulative consumption and cost","when":"The user submits feeding date, pen, lot, ration, planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, and status"},{"given":"A feeding activity has planned quantity 100 pounds and actual delivered quantity 115 pounds","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"unit","then":"The returned variance value is 15 pounds","when":"The web app calculates the feed variance"},{"given":"A saved feeding activity response includes updated stock and lot totals","id":"AC-REQ-9.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned inventory quantity after consumption and the returned cumulative lot consumption and cost","when":"The user views the activity and its lot"},{"given":"A feeding activity would exceed the available ingredient stock and the service refuses the save","id":"AC-REQ-9.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned stock error and does not show the activity as saved","when":"The user submits the activity"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let operational users record feeding activity by pen and lot and display the returned variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, feeding status, and lot-level consumption and cost totals.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-4","ASM-9","ASM-10","ASM-11","ASM-28","ASM-31","ASM-32","ASM-34","Q-5"],"stability":0.8},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has livestock or operations permission and opens a lot's weight screen","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned measurement including total lot weight, weight gain since the prior measurement, and the new entry in the lot's chronological history","when":"The user submits measurement date, number of animals weighed, average animal weight, and notes"},{"given":"A user lacks permission to add weight measurements","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the measurement history and does not show an add-measurement action","when":"The user opens a lot's weight screen"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let users with livestock or operations permission add lot weight measurements and display each lot's measurement history as a time series.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-12","Q-8"],"stability":0.8},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has receiving date 2026-01-01, entry average weight 400 pounds, current average weight 500 pounds, target weight 600 pounds, current date 2026-01-11, and feeding records totaling 1200 pounds and 2400 dollars","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"unit","then":"The returned metrics contain 10 days on feed, 100 pounds total weight gain, 10 pounds average daily gain, 1200 pounds total feed consumed, FCR 12, cost of gain 24 dollars per pound, and projected ship date 2026-01-21","when":"A test calls the public lot-metrics calculation method"},{"given":"A lot has no positive ADG","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows projected ship date as unavailable","when":"The user opens the lot performance screen"},{"given":"A feeding or weight record is saved and the service returns updated records","id":"AC-REQ-11.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the recalculated metric values from the updated records","when":"The user opens or refreshes the lot performance screen"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall calculate lot feed-to-gain metrics from receiving, weight, and feeding records and refresh the displayed metrics when a feeding or weight record changes.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-13","ASM-20","ASM-33"],"stability":0.76},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The dashboard service returns the current yard, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, weight, and lot performance values","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows active lot and pen counts, animals per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, total gain, ADG, feed-to-gain ratio, cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots","when":"A user opens the dashboard"},{"given":"The dashboard displays best- and worst-performing lot rankings","id":"AC-REQ-12.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the lot ranking and the selected measure as its basis","when":"The user selects FCR, ADG, or cost of gain as the ranking measure"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display a dashboard with yard and lot performance values for active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory, ration usage, bunk rates, planned and actual feed, feed consumption and cost, weights, gain, ADG, FCR, cost of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-14","ASM-22","ASM-36"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The operational report service returns records for multiple pens, lots, rations, feed plans, inventory items, and feed costs","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows which pen consumed the most feed, which lot has the best FCR and highest ADG, which ration is used most, planned-versus-actual feed and over- or under-feeding pens, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain","when":"A user opens the reports screen and applies its available filters"},{"given":"The filtered operational report is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-13.2","level":"ui","then":"The downloaded file contains the filtered report rows shown on the screen","when":"The user exports the report as CSV"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide filterable operational reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability that answer the requested pen, lot, ration, plan-variance, inventory, and cost-of-gain questions.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-17"],"stability":0.76},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns records for authorized and unauthorized yards and the user's permissions allow only a subset of yards and profitability fields","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows only the authorized-yard records and only the profitability fields allowed by the returned permissions","when":"The user opens a dashboard or report"},{"given":"A user exports a filtered dashboard or report view","id":"AC-REQ-14.2","level":"ui","then":"The downloaded file contains only the authorized-yard records and profitability fields shown to that user","when":"The export is generated"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall present dashboards, operational reports, and feed-to-gain report results and exports only for yards and profitability fields allowed by the signed-in user's returned permissions.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-10","Q-1","ASM-14"],"stability":0.82},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has weight-gain trends for which the insights service returns a feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestion","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the suggestion and the trend data or rule cited as its basis","when":"The user opens the lot insights"},{"given":"A suggestion is displayed and the user has not chosen an action","id":"AC-REQ-15.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the saved feed plan unchanged","when":"The user views the suggestion"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall present explainable rule-based suggestions for feeding adjustments or sale timing from weight-gain trends and shall leave the decision to act to the user.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-8","I-9","ASM-18","ASM-19"],"stability":0.76},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The report service returns lot records with weight and feeding data for a selected date range","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows matching lots with ADG, FCR, and cost-of-gain values calculated from records in the selected date range","when":"The user opens the feed-to-gain report and applies date-range, breed, sex, or pen filters"},{"given":"Records without sex data are included in the report result set","id":"AC-REQ-16.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the sex filter as unavailable for records without sex data","when":"The user views the sex filter"},{"given":"The user has applied report filters","id":"AC-REQ-16.3","level":"ui","then":"Each downloaded file contains the filtered report rows shown on the screen","when":"The user exports the report as CSV and as PDF"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide a feed-to-gain report that compares lot ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, filters results by date range, breed, sex, or pen, and exports the filtered results as CSV or PDF.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","ASM-21","ASM-35","Q-1"],"stability":0.8},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Sample data is available and has not been loaded","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the loaded records as sample data and distinguishes them from operational records","when":"An authorized user loads the sample data"},{"given":"The sample data is already loaded","id":"AC-REQ-17.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a duplicate-load message and the returned record list contains no duplicate sample records","when":"A user attempts to load it again"},{"given":"A user starts a sample-data reset or replacement","id":"AC-REQ-17.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the existing sample records unchanged","when":"The confirmation dialog is displayed and the user cancels"},{"given":"A user starts a sample-data reset or replacement","id":"AC-REQ-17.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned sample-data state","when":"The user confirms and the service returns the reset result"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let an authorized user load visibly distinct sample data, prevent duplicate sample loading, and require confirmation before a sample-data reset or replacement.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-12","ASM-15","ASM-37"],"stability":0.78},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The summary service returns active-lot values and aggregate ADG, cost of gain, and feed cost","id":"AC-REQ-18.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost for the returned active lots","when":"A user with yard-summary permission opens the yard summary"},{"given":"The summary service returns no data for one or more summary fields","id":"AC-REQ-18.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned available values and an explicit unavailable value for each missing field","when":"A user opens the yard summary"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display a yard-level summary of active-lot total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","ASM-16","ASM-38"],"stability":0.76},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivery overview page is available","id":"AC-REQ-19.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows sections for the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis","when":"A user opens the page"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide a delivery overview page containing the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"],"stability":0.72}],"suggestions":["Agree and version the web/API response contracts for permissions, forecast values, stock errors, report exports, and calculated metrics so the UI behaviors can be tested against stable fixtures."]},{"assumptions":["ASM-1 and ASM-23: The demo imports mock source records through a documented adapter; no live procurement connector is specified.","ASM-2 and ASM-25: Lots may occupy multiple pens, and animal quantities are retained for PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen mappings.","ASM-3: Yard target-weight and gain-rate defaults apply unless a lot-specific override is supplied.","ASM-4 and ASM-28: Wastage applies to estimates and projections; actual stock consumption follows delivered quantity, with known wastage represented separately.","ASM-5 and ASM-29: Ration results show candidate-mix nutrition and cost; optimization identifies the lowest-cost mix meeting selected requirements, and saving remains a user choice.","ASM-7 and ASM-30: Changed plan inputs leave a saved plan unchanged and flag it for authorized review, confirmation, or regeneration.","ASM-9 and ASM-31: A stock-insufficient feeding response blocks saving until stock is sufficient or an authorized adjustment is made.","ASM-13 and ASM-33: Projected ship date uses the current date and positive ADG, and is unavailable without positive ADG.","ASM-18: Insights are explainable rule-based suggestions and do not apply changes without user action.","ASM-20 and ASM-34: Plans and feeding use as-fed quantities; feed totals use pounds for feed-to-gain, nutrition uses dry matter, and dry-matter values are reported separately.","ASM-21: Report metrics use feeding and weight records within the selected date range and relevant starting and ending weights.","ASM-22: Users select the dashboard lot-ranking measure from FCR, ADG, or cost of gain.","ASM-35: Sex is retained when provided by the source and is unavailable for records without sex data.","ASM-37: Sample records remain distinct from operational records and reset or replacement requires confirmation.","ASM-38: Yard summary ADG and cost of gain use aggregate gain and aggregate feed cost across included active lots."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths 320 px, 768 px, and 1280 px, horizontal page overflow is 0 px; at 320 px width, each touch control is at least 44 × 44 CSS px.","text":"Every web page shall remain usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page scrolling, and touch controls at the narrow viewport shall have a minimum target size of 44 by 44 CSS pixels."}],"outOfScope":["API-SIDE: durable persistence and database migration behavior for imported records, mappings, inventory, rations, plans, feeding events, and weight measurements.","API-SIDE: authoritative calculation and update rules for inventory movements, ration nutrition and cost, feed-plan quantities, lot rollups, forecast values, and feed-to-gain metrics; the web requirements cover displayed API responses and UI reactions.","API-SIDE: authorization enforcement, import identifier matching and deduplication, stock sufficiency decisions, and authoritative yard/profitability data filtering; the web requirements cover controls, displayed responses, and export contents."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"the sign-in request contains the submitted email and password and the screen displays the destination page when the response indicates success","when":"the user submits an email address and password"},{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the response error message","when":"the user submits credentials and the response indicates refusal"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in and display the result of each sign-in attempt.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operational user is viewing the import screen with mock source records available","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the available vendor, cost, head count, weight, breed, age, and source fields","when":"the user reviews the records"},{"given":"An operational user has reviewed mock source records","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"ui","then":"the import request contains the selected source records and the screen displays the response status and imported-record list","when":"the user submits the import"},{"given":"A user without operational access is viewing imported records","id":"AC-REQ-2.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the records for viewing and does not display an enabled import control","when":"the user opens the import screen"}],"ears":"When an operational user starts a mock-data import, the web app shall let the user review and submit procurement and receiving records containing vendor, costs, head count, weights, breed, age, and source data.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-23","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operational user is viewing an imported PO line","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the PO-line, lot, and pen relationships with the entered animal allocation quantities","when":"the user maps the line to one or more lots and maps a lot to one or more pens"},{"given":"A mapping response includes pen information","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each mapped pen's ID, capacity, current animal count, and mapped allocation quantity","when":"the mapping screen renders the response"},{"given":"A user without operational access is viewing mappings","id":"AC-REQ-3.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays existing mappings and does not display enabled mapping-edit controls","when":"the user opens the mapping screen"}],"ears":"When an operational user edits entity mappings, the web app shall provide PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen mapping controls that retain allocated animal quantities and display pen capacity and current animal counts.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-2","ASM-25","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The import response identifies source records as matched to existing records","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the matched record list and the response status without displaying those records as newly created duplicates","when":"the repeated import completes"}],"ears":"When an operational user repeats an import containing previously imported source-system identifiers, the web app shall display the import result for the corresponding records returned by the import service.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-24","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The forecast response contains incoming animal data, yard defaults, and forecast values","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each lot's incoming data, target weight, expected gain rate, and projected market date","when":"a user opens the forecast screen"},{"given":"An authorized manager is viewing forecast assumptions","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"ui","then":"the forecast request contains the changed value and the screen displays the response status and returned forecast values","when":"the manager changes a yard default or lot-specific override and submits it"},{"given":"A user without manager authorization is viewing forecast assumptions","id":"AC-REQ-5.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays forecast values and does not display enabled assumption-edit controls","when":"the user opens the forecast screen"}],"ears":"The web app shall display market-date and target-weight forecasts based on incoming animal data and allow authorized managers to view and change yard defaults and lot-specific overrides for target weight and expected gain rate.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-3","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized inventory user is viewing the inventory screen","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays item name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry matter percentage, energy value, storage location, wastage setting, and the response status","when":"the user opens an item or submits an item, receipt, adjustment, or wastage change"},{"given":"The inventory response contains movement data","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays opening stock, stock received, stock consumed, and closing stock for each feed item","when":"the inventory screen renders the response"},{"given":"A user with inventory viewing access but without inventory-edit access is viewing inventory","id":"AC-REQ-6.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays inventory details and does not display enabled item, receipt, adjustment, or wastage-edit controls","when":"the user opens an item"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide inventory screens for authorized inventory users to maintain feed items, record receipts and adjustments, and configure wastage, and shall display inventory item details and stock movements to users with inventory viewing access.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-28","ASM-34","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The projection response contains available stock, upcoming feed plans, and wastage-adjusted estimates","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays projected inventory for the daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons and displays the configured wastage ratio","when":"a user opens inventory projections"},{"given":"The projection response has no saved upcoming feed plans for an item","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the response's empty-data state for that item's projected inventory","when":"a user opens inventory projections"}],"ears":"The web app shall display feed-inventory projections for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons using upcoming saved feed plans and the configured wastage ratio.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized ration manager is creating or revising a ration","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays ration name, type, ingredients, proportions, dry matter, energy, cost per unit, and intended animal type or weight range","when":"the manager enters ration details and ingredient proportions"},{"given":"The ration response contains nutrition values and calculated ingredient-mix cost","id":"AC-REQ-8.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned nutrition values and calculated cost per pound","when":"the ration screen renders the response"},{"given":"An authorized ration manager has selected nutrition requirements and candidate mixes","id":"AC-REQ-8.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned candidate mix results, their nutrition values and costs, and the lowest-cost result that meets the selected requirements","when":"the manager requests optimization"},{"given":"A user without ration-management access is viewing a ration","id":"AC-REQ-8.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the ration and does not display enabled create, revise, optimize, or approve controls","when":"the user opens the ration screen"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide authorized ration managers with controls to create and revise rations, view their nutrition and ingredient-mix cost, compare candidate mixes against selected nutrition requirements, and choose whether to save an optimized mix.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-5","ASM-6","ASM-29","ASM-34","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized planner is creating a feed plan","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"the plan request contains those values and the screen displays the returned planned quantity, quantity per animal, feeding time, feed cost, expected energy intake, and status","when":"the planner selects a date, pen, bunk rate, ration, and animal count and submits the plan"},{"given":"A saved plan is flagged for review after its pen count, bunk rate, or ration assignment changes","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the unchanged saved plan and a review flag","when":"a user opens the plan"},{"given":"An authorized planner is viewing a plan flagged for review","id":"AC-REQ-9.3","level":"ui","then":"the plan request contains the selected confirmation or regeneration action and the screen displays the response status and returned plan","when":"the planner confirms an update or regenerates the plan"},{"given":"An operator is assigned to a pen","id":"AC-REQ-9.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays execution-status controls for that plan and does not display enabled plan-generation or plan-adjustment controls","when":"the operator views a plan for that pen"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide authorized planners with controls to generate and adjust pen-level feed plans from a date, pen bunk rate, selected ration, and animal count, and shall display plan quantities, per-animal quantities, feeding time, feed cost, expected energy intake, and execution status.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-7","ASM-8","ASM-20","ASM-30","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operator is recording feeding activity for a pen","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"the feeding request contains the entered values and the screen displays the response status and returned event fields","when":"the operator enters feeding date, lot, ration, planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, and feeding status and submits the event"},{"given":"A successful feeding response contains calculated values","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays variance as actual feed quantity minus planned feed quantity, feed cost, energy value, inventory consumed by ingredient, and cumulative lot feed consumption and cost","when":"the event screen renders the response"},{"given":"A feeding response refuses an event because available stock is insufficient","id":"AC-REQ-10.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the response error and does not display the event as saved","when":"the operator submits the event"},{"given":"A feeding response includes actual delivered quantity and an inventory movement","id":"AC-REQ-10.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays inventory consumption for the delivered quantity and displays known wastage as a separate movement rather than added delivered feed","when":"the event screen renders the response"},{"given":"A saved plan and a feeding response contain different planned and actual quantities","id":"AC-REQ-10.5","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays actual intake and variance and provides an enabled control to adjust a future plan without changing the saved plan","when":"an authorized user views feeding activity"}],"ears":"When an operator records feeding activity, the web app shall provide a pen-level entry screen for planned and delivered feed data and display the returned variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, and lot consumption totals.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-5","I-6","ASM-4","ASM-9","ASM-10","ASM-11","ASM-19","ASM-28","ASM-31","ASM-32","ASM-34","Q-5","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized user is viewing a lot's weight screen","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"ui","then":"the measurement request contains lot, date, animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight, and notes, and the screen displays the response status","when":"the user enters measurement details and submits them"},{"given":"The weight response contains multiple measurements","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned measurements in date order with weight gain since the previous measurement where returned","when":"a user views the lot's weight history"},{"given":"A user without measurement-entry access is viewing a lot","id":"AC-REQ-11.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the measurement time series and does not display an enabled add-measurement control","when":"the user opens its weight history"}],"ears":"When an authorized livestock or operations user records a lot weight measurement, the web app shall provide fields for measurement date, animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight, and notes, and shall display the returned measurement history as a time series.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-12","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The lot metrics response contains receiving date, entry and current average weight, feed totals, feed cost, target weight, ADG, and projected ship date","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed in pounds, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date from the response","when":"a user opens lot performance"},{"given":"A saved feeding or weight event returns updated lot metrics","id":"AC-REQ-12.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the updated metric values returned for the lot","when":"the event save completes"},{"given":"The metrics response indicates that positive ADG is unavailable","id":"AC-REQ-12.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the projected ship date as unavailable","when":"a user views lot performance"}],"ears":"The web app shall display returned lot feed-to-gain metrics for days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed in pounds, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date, and shall refresh those displayed metrics after a feeding or weight event is saved.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-6","I-8","ASM-13","ASM-20","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The insights response contains a suggestion and its weight-gain basis","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the suggestion and the returned basis for it without changing a feed plan or sale date","when":"a user opens lot insights"},{"given":"A user chooses to act on a displayed suggestion","id":"AC-REQ-13.2","level":"ui","then":"the change request contains the user's selected action and the screen displays the response status","when":"the user submits the corresponding change"}],"ears":"The web app shall display explainable rule-based feeding-adjustment or sale-timing suggestions based on lot weight-gain trends and require a user action before applying a suggestion.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-8","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The dashboard response contains yard, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, weight, and performance values","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays active lot and pen counts, animals per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, total weight gain, ADG, feed-to-gain ratio, feed cost per unit of gain, and energy consumed","when":"a user opens the dashboard"},{"given":"The dashboard contains performance values for multiple lots","id":"AC-REQ-14.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays best- and worst-performing lots and the selected ranking basis","when":"a user selects FCR, ADG, or cost of gain as the ranking measure"},{"given":"A dashboard response contains no values for a summary field","id":"AC-REQ-14.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned empty-data state for that field","when":"a user opens the dashboard"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide dashboards and reports showing returned yard and lot performance data for active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory status, ration usage, bunk rates, planned and actual feed, feed totals and costs, weight gain, ADG, feed-to-gain, cost of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-14","ASM-22","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The access response identifies authorized yards and restricted profitability fields","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays only authorized-yard records and omits restricted profitability values","when":"a user views dashboards and reports"},{"given":"A user exports displayed dashboard or report data","id":"AC-REQ-15.2","level":"ui","then":"the file contains only authorized-yard records and profitability fields permitted for that user","when":"the export file is generated"}],"ears":"Where yard and profitability access restrictions apply, the web app shall display only dashboard and report results and export data authorized for the user's yards and profitability permissions.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-10","Q-1","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user is viewing the feed-to-gain report","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"ui","then":"the report request contains the selected filters and the screen displays the returned lot comparisons for ADG, FCR, and cost of gain","when":"the user selects date range, breed, sex, or pen filters"},{"given":"The report data has no sex value for some records","id":"AC-REQ-16.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the sex filter as unavailable for those records and displays the returned report values","when":"a user views the sex filter and those records"},{"given":"A user has filtered feed-to-gain report results","id":"AC-REQ-16.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen downloads a file in the selected format containing the filtered report results","when":"the user selects CSV or PDF export"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide a feed-to-gain report with lot comparisons for ADG, FCR, and cost of gain and filters for date range, breed, sex, and pen, and shall allow CSV and PDF exports of the filtered results.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","ASM-21","ASM-35","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens the sample-data screen before sample data is loaded","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the resulting sample records with a visible sample-data designation","when":"the user loads the provided sample data"},{"given":"Sample data is already loaded","id":"AC-REQ-17.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the existing sample-data status and does not offer a duplicate-load action as an enabled control","when":"a user opens the sample-data screen"},{"given":"A user requests reset or replacement of sample data","id":"AC-REQ-17.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays a confirmation prompt and the reset or replacement request is not sent","when":"the user has not confirmed the action"},{"given":"A user confirms a sample-data reset or replacement","id":"AC-REQ-17.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the response status and resulting sample-data list","when":"the action completes"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide controls to load sample data that remains visibly distinct from operational data and to reset or replace sample data only after user confirmation.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-12","ASM-15","ASM-37"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The yard summary response contains active-lot aggregate values","id":"AC-REQ-18.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost","when":"a user opens the yard-level summary"},{"given":"The yard summary response contains no data for a summary metric","id":"AC-REQ-18.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned missing-data state for that metric","when":"a user opens the yard-level summary"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide a yard-level summary dashboard showing aggregate total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost across active lots.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","ASM-16","ASM-38"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens the presentation page","id":"AC-REQ-19.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, go-to-market analysis, and overview prompt and other prompts","when":"the page renders"}],"ears":"The web app shall provide a presentation page containing the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, an app demo, the testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, go-to-market analysis, and the overview prompt and other prompts used.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]}],"suggestions":["After the procurement system and its interface are identified, consider replacing the demo mock-data adapter with a live connector."]},{"assumptions":["ASM-1 and ASM-23: procurement and receiving ingestion uses a documented mock-data adapter; a live source connector awaits identification of the source interface.","ASM-2 and ASM-25: allocations retain animal quantities across PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen relationships, including splits.","ASM-3: forecasts use configurable yard target-weight and expected-gain defaults with optional lot-specific overrides.","ASM-4, ASM-27, and ASM-28: wastage affects estimates and projections based on saved plans; actual stock consumption uses delivered feed and known actual wastage is a separate movement.","ASM-5 and ASM-29: optimization compares candidate mixes against user-selected nutrition requirements, highlights the lowest-cost qualifying mix, and saves only when selected.","ASM-7 and ASM-30: changed plan inputs flag the saved plan for review; its values remain unchanged until an authorized planner confirms an update or regenerates it.","ASM-9 and ASM-31: insufficient stock causes the API to refuse the feeding event; the web app presents the refusal.","ASM-13 and ASM-33: projected ship date uses current date plus (target weight minus current weight) divided by positive ADG and is unavailable without positive ADG.","ASM-18 and ASM-19: predictive insights are explainable rule-based suggestions; intake variance is shown without automatically rewriting a saved plan.","ASM-20 and ASM-34: plan and delivered-feed quantities use as-fed units, feed totals convert to pounds for feed-to-gain metrics, and nutrition uses dry matter.","ASM-21: report metrics use records and relevant starting and ending weights within the selected date range.","ASM-22: users choose the measure used to rank best- and worst-performing lots.","ASM-35: sex is retained when provided by the source and the sex filter is unavailable for records without sex.","ASM-36: dashboards are summary-only; lot and report screens provide detail.","ASM-37 and ASM-15: sample records remain distinct from operational records, duplicate load results are surfaced, and reset requires confirmation.","ASM-38: yard summary average ADG and cost of gain use aggregate total gain and total feed cost across included active lots.","ASM-17: lot profitability is presented as an on-screen filtered list with CSV export rather than a custom report builder.","The separate API is authoritative for server-side calculations and permissions; this web app displays returned values and refusal messages."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"0 horizontal overflow at viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1440 CSS px; primary touch controls are at least 44 × 44 CSS px at 320 CSS px.","text":"Every web-app page shall render without horizontal page overflow at phone, tablet, and desktop reference widths."}],"outOfScope":[],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the signed-in landing page returned for that user","when":"The user submits an email address and password accepted by the sign-in API"},{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"ui","then":"An authentication error message is shown on the screen","when":"The sign-in API refuses the submitted credentials"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password, the web app shall send those credentials to the sign-in API and show the signed-in operational pages or the returned authentication error.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2"],"stability":0.96},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operationally authorized user opens the import screen with mock adapter data available","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the vendor, cost, head-count, weight, breed, age, source, purchase-order, and receiving fields","when":"The user previews the source records"},{"given":"An operationally authorized user has selected source records","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the import result returned by the API, including created or updated record counts when supplied","when":"The user submits the import"},{"given":"A user without operational access opens the import screen","id":"AC-REQ-2.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows imported records without an import submission control","when":"The screen is displayed"}],"ears":"Where procurement and receiving import is available, the web app shall let operationally authorized users load the documented mock-data adapter, inspect vendor, cost, head-count, weight, breed, age, source, purchase-order, and receiving fields, and submit selected source records for import.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-3","ASM-1","ASM-23"],"stability":0.91},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The mapping screen receives a PO line allocated to multiple lots and a lot allocated to multiple pens","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen relationship with its allocated animal quantity","when":"The screen renders the returned mappings"},{"given":"An operationally authorized user changes mapping quantities","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved mapping values returned by the API","when":"The user saves the mappings"},{"given":"A user without operational access opens the mapping screen","id":"AC-REQ-3.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows mapping records without mapping edit controls","when":"The screen is displayed"}],"ears":"When an operationally authorized user saves mapping allocations, the web app shall submit and display traceable PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen relationships with allocated animal quantities, including one PO line split across multiple lots and a lot allocated across multiple pens.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-3","ASM-2","ASM-25"],"stability":0.92},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The forecast response contains incoming animal data, yard defaults, and a lot-specific override","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the projected market date and target weight using the lot-specific override","when":"The user opens the lot forecast"},{"given":"A lot forecast has no positive gain rate available","id":"AC-REQ-4.2","level":"ui","then":"The projected date field displays an unavailable value on the screen","when":"The user opens the forecast"},{"given":"An authorized manager opens the forecast settings","id":"AC-REQ-4.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows editable yard defaults and lot-specific override fields","when":"The screen is displayed"},{"given":"A user who is not an authorized manager opens the forecast settings","id":"AC-REQ-4.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows forecast values without assumption-edit controls","when":"The screen is displayed"}],"ears":"Where lifecycle forecasts are displayed, the web app shall show projected market dates and target weights based on incoming animal data and configured yard defaults, use lot-specific overrides when present, show a forecast as unavailable when no positive gain rate is available, and expose assumption-edit controls only to authorized managers.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-4","ASM-3","ASM-33"],"stability":0.88},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The inventory response contains feed items and stock movements","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the requested item fields and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values","when":"The user opens the inventory screen"},{"given":"An authorized inventory user opens an inventory item","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays controls for those inventory changes","when":"The user selects receipt, adjustment, or wastage settings"},{"given":"A user without authorized inventory access opens an inventory item","id":"AC-REQ-5.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays inventory values without receipt, adjustment, or wastage-setting controls","when":"The screen is displayed"}],"ears":"Where inventory is displayed, the web app shall show each feed item's name, category, available quantity, unit of measure, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values, and expose receipt, adjustment, and wastage-setting controls only to authorized inventory users.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-5","ASM-4","ASM-34"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The inventory projection screen is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen lists daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual projection values","when":"The user opens the horizon selector"},{"given":"The API returns projections based on upcoming plans and a configured wastage ratio","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned projected consumption and remaining inventory values","when":"The user selects a projection horizon"},{"given":"The API returns a known actual wastage movement","id":"AC-REQ-6.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen lists actual wastage as a separate movement from delivered feed consumption","when":"The user views inventory movements"}],"ears":"Where inventory projections are displayed, the web app shall offer daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons and show projected consumption based on saved upcoming feed plans with the configured wastage ratio, while presenting known actual wastage as a separate stock movement.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-27","ASM-28"],"stability":0.88},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized ration manager opens ration management","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays fields for ingredients, proportions, ration type, intended animal type or weight range, dry matter, energy, and cost per pound","when":"The user creates or revises a ration"},{"given":"The API returns candidate mixes and nutrition requirements selected by the user","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen identifies the lowest-cost returned mix that satisfies the selected requirements and shows its nutrition and cost values","when":"The user runs optimization"},{"given":"An optimized candidate is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-7.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the candidate without showing it as a saved ration","when":"The user has not selected a save action"},{"given":"A user without authorized ration-management access opens ration management","id":"AC-REQ-7.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows existing rations without create, revise, optimize, or approve controls","when":"The screen is displayed"}],"ears":"Where ration management is available, the web app shall let authorized ration managers create, revise, optimize, and approve rations, display ingredient proportions, ration type, intended animal type or weight range, dry-matter and energy values, and cost per pound, and present the lowest-cost candidate mix that satisfies user-selected nutrition requirements without saving it until selected by the user.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-6","ASM-5","ASM-20","ASM-29"],"stability":0.89},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized planner has selected a date, pen, bunk rate, ration, and animal count","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned planned quantity, quantity per animal, total cost, expected energy, and plan status with the selected pen, date, lots, and ration","when":"The planner generates the feed plan"},{"given":"A user without planning access opens feed planning","id":"AC-REQ-8.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows existing plans without plan-generation controls","when":"The screen is displayed"}],"ears":"When an authorized planner generates a feed plan for a date and pen, the web app shall submit the daily bunk rate, selected ration, and animal count and display the returned plan's pen, assigned lots, animal count, ration, planned quantity, planned time, quantity per animal, total cost, expected energy, and execution status.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-7","ASM-8","ASM-20"],"stability":0.9},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A saved plan's bunk rate, animal count, or ration assignment has changed since generation","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen flags the plan for review and displays its previously saved values","when":"The user opens the plan"},{"given":"An authorized planner opens a plan flagged for review","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows confirm-update and regenerate controls","when":"The screen is displayed"},{"given":"An operator assigned to the plan's pen opens the plan","id":"AC-REQ-9.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned status value","when":"The operator updates its execution status"},{"given":"Actual bunk intake differs from the saved plan","id":"AC-REQ-9.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays actual intake and variance while the saved plan values remain unchanged","when":"The user views the feeding plan and activity"}],"ears":"While a saved plan's bunk rate, animal count, or ration assignment differs from its generation inputs, the web app shall flag the plan for review, retain its saved values, expose authorized planner controls to confirm an update or regenerate it, allow assigned-pen operators to update execution status, and show intake variance without automatically rewriting the saved plan.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-7","ASM-7","ASM-19","ASM-30"],"stability":0.89},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operational user enters feeding activity and the API accepts it","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved event, its actual-minus-planned variance, feed cost, energy, inventory consumption, and returned lot consumption totals","when":"The user saves the activity"},{"given":"The API accepts a feeding event with a delivered quantity","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays stock consumption based on the delivered quantity without adding wastage to that actual movement","when":"The user views the returned inventory movement"},{"given":"The API refuses a feeding event because available stock is insufficient","id":"AC-REQ-10.3","level":"ui","then":"An insufficient-stock error message is shown on the screen","when":"The user saves the activity"},{"given":"A user without operational access opens feeding activity","id":"AC-REQ-10.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows existing activity without controls to record a feeding event","when":"The screen is displayed"}],"ears":"When an operational user records feeding activity, the web app shall submit the feeding date, pen, lot, ration, planned and delivered quantities, and status, show the actual-minus-planned variance and returned feed cost, energy, inventory consumption, and lot consumption totals, and display the returned stock-control error when the API refuses an event for insufficient stock.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-5","ASM-9","ASM-11","ASM-20","ASM-28","ASM-31"],"stability":0.92},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has returned weight measurements","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the measurements in time order with their returned measurement fields","when":"The user opens its weight history"},{"given":"An authorized livestock or operations user enters a weight measurement","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved measurement in the lot's time series","when":"The user submits the measurement"},{"given":"A user without weight-entry access opens the lot history","id":"AC-REQ-11.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows measurement history without an add-measurement control","when":"The screen is displayed"}],"ears":"Where lot weight history is displayed, the web app shall show a time-ordered series of measurements and let authorized livestock or operations users submit a measurement containing lot, date, animals weighed, average weight, total lot weight, gain since the prior measurement, and not